Car_1pt_Motion_3D: Calc_Object_Angles must read the MulMatrix0 result (local_a0)

asm 0x4403be/0x4403d9: gte_MulMatrix0 writes its result matrix to [ebp-0x9c] and
the following Calc_Object_Angles reads the SAME [ebp-0x9c]. Ghidra emitted
Calc_Object_Angles(local_80, &local_50) -- local_80 is never written on this
path, so the landed-car angles came from stack garbage. This was the remaining
L2 frame-0x88 native/wasm splitter (watchpoint/FR chain: identical entry state,
0x792a04 = (int)sStack_18<<12 diverged 0x0 vs 0xffeaa000; sStack_18 derives
from _ang3[1] = Calc_Object_Angles output). Wrong-buffer class (cousin of the
scattered-locals class; the asm-recovery comment at the gte_MulMatrix0 call
already documented [ebp-0x9c] as the product buffer).

--- a/dd2.c
+++ b/dd2.c
@@ -29881,7 +29881,7 @@
       iVar7 = param_1 * 0x27c;
       Calc_Object_Angles((short *)(iVar7 + 0x78a754),(short *)(&DAT_0078a790 + iVar7));
       gte_MulMatrix0((undefined4 *)(local_34 + 0x50),(short *)(iVar7 + 0x78a754),(undefined4 *)local_a0);  /* asm 0x4403be: lea eax,[ebp-0x9c] */
-      Calc_Object_Angles(local_80,&local_50);
+      Calc_Object_Angles(local_a0,&local_50);  /* asm 0x4403d9: lea eax,[ebp-0x9c] -- reads the SAME buffer gte_MulMatrix0 just wrote (local_a0); Ghidra passed the never-written local_80 -> landing angles from stack garbage (THE L2 frame-0x88 native/wasm splitter: 0x792a04 got (int)garbage<<12) */
       local_50 = local_50 - *(short *)(&DAT_0078a790 + iVar7);
       sStack_18 = sStack_4e - *(short *)(&DAT_0078a792 + iVar7);
       local_4c = local_4c - *(short *)(iVar7 + 0x78a794);
